WEBVTT

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.410
My name is Bryan Mey. I'm the president of the Friends of Lums Pond.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.650
I initially joined about five years ago.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:16.570
Quickly fell in love with the volunteer work and have just been kind of diving headfirst into

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.050
trying to help out the park as much as I can.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.490
It's hard to describe how far we've come.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:28.170
We've done so much stuff from trail cleanups to member socials.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:34.670
As big as like now we've got our big annual fundraiser that we call Pond Fest right over

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.090
there in Area 1.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.850
Huge success the first two years.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.810
We had 1,500 people show up last year, which was amazing.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.330
Raised about $18,000, which is just phenomenal.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.030
The community has been amazing.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:52.490
And that's been what our efforts have been really is trying to channel the community.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:58.070
A lot of people love this park and we're just trying to be the bridge that connects the community

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.490
to the park.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:09.690
What 75 years means to me is that we've successfully created a protection of this beautiful nature

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.610
that we all love across Delaware.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:16.450
And we just need to keep protecting it and keep putting things in place that help us sustain

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.590
and maintain the beauty that is Delaware State Parks.
